---
globs: test/**/*_test.rb
alwaysApply: true
---

[LANG][!RUBY] This is a Ruby on Rails project. All tests use Minitest with ActiveSupport::TestCase.

[TEST][!TIGHT] Write unit tests that are tight, isolated, and follow best practices in Ruby development.

[SPEED][!PROFILE] EVERY test MUST declare a speed_profile before the test definition:
  - speed_profile :fast (< 10 seconds) - Unit tests, validations, pure logic
  - speed_profile :medium (< 60 seconds) - LLM calls, tool execution, file I/O
  - speed_profile :slow (< 120 seconds) - Workers, workflows, integration tests
  
[SPEED][!ENFORCE] Tests will FAIL if they exceed their speed profile SLA. Choose appropriately.

[SPEED][!PER-TEST] Speed profiles are declared PER TEST, not per file:
  ```ruby
  class MyTest < ActiveSupport::TestCase
    speed_profile :fast
    test "quick validation" do
      assert true
    end
    
    speed_profile :medium
    test "with LLM call" do
      result = service.call_llm
      assert result.present?
    end
  end
  ```

[NAMING][!NO-PHASES] Never name tests after phases or milestones. Test names should be informative.

[NO-MOCK][!REAL] Never mock or stub. Prefer testing real implementations with real or seeded data. If an external system is unavailable, skip or fail explicitly—do not replace with fakes.

[SCOPE][!FOCUSED] Keep tests tight and focused. Each test should validate a single behavior or responsibility. Do not combine multiple concerns in a single test.

[ISOLATION][!CLEAN] Ensure test isolation. Test suites must not depend on shared state. Each test should set up and tear down its own context cleanly and independently.

[RUBY][!IDIOMATIC] Use standard Ruby testing practices with Minitest. Follow Rails conventions and use FactoryBot for test data.

[QUALITY][!READABLE] Write clear, readable code. Maintain high code quality within tests, just as in production code. Use descriptive names, consistent formatting, and minimal duplication.

[ASSERT][!MEANINGFUL] Aim for meaningful assertions. Tests should fail only when the behavior under test is incorrect, and the failure message should clearly indicate what went wrong.

[PERF][!NO-SLEEPS] Avoid sleeps where possible. Use real timing only when testing actual performance.

[INTEGRATION][!WHEN-READY] At the end of a feature set create integration tests where they make sense. Mark them as :slow and ensure they pass.

[WORKFLOW][!TEST-LOOP] Follow the testing workflow:
  - During development: ruby lib/test_runner.rb --speed fast (runs in ~5 seconds)
  - Testing new features: Run fast tests + tests for modified files
  - Before PR/merge: ruby lib/test_runner.rb --speed all (runs full suite)

[DATA][!REAL-DATA] Use real data and factories. Create tests with actual data, not mocks or stubs.

[FRONTEND][!SEPARATE] For frontend testing, see rules/frontend-testing-rule.mdc

